{
  "case_id": "2021-20-637",
  "document_hash": "59b49428ee030541a5a545308836d6a29999e9b1d0be7442b0acfea8b82e6ba4",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Hemphill",
      "case_id": "2021-20-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "59b49428ee030541a5a545308836d6a29999e9b1d0be7442b0acfea8b82e6ba4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59b49428ee03-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Hemphill premised his closing argument, like the rest of his defense, on the theory that Morris was the shooter."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "59b49428ee030541a5a545308836d6a29999e9b1d0be7442b0acfea8b82e6ba4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59b49428ee03-0001-0000",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Accordingly, the Court turns to the merits of that claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Hemphill",
      "case_id": "2021-20-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "59b49428ee030541a5a545308836d6a29999e9b1d0be7442b0acfea8b82e6ba4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59b49428ee03-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Hemphill timely objected that admission of the plea allocution would be \u201ca Crawford violation.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-20-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "59b49428ee030541a5a545308836d6a29999e9b1d0be7442b0acfea8b82e6ba4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59b49428ee03-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One of the bedrock constitutional protections afforded to criminal defendants is the Confrontation Clause of the Sixth Amendment, which states: \u201cIn all criminal prosecutions, the accused shall enjoy the right . . . to be confronted with the witnesses against him.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State",
      "case_id": "2021-20-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "59b49428ee030541a5a545308836d6a29999e9b1d0be7442b0acfea8b82e6ba4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59b49428ee03-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The State's primary contention is that the Reid rule \u201cis not an exception to the Confrontation Clause at all.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "59b49428ee030541a5a545308836d6a29999e9b1d0be7442b0acfea8b82e6ba4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59b49428ee03-0002-0001",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Under New York case law, a trial court may generally admit otherwise inadmissible evidence if a party has \u201copened the door\u201d to its introduction at trial."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "59b49428ee030541a5a545308836d6a29999e9b1d0be7442b0acfea8b82e6ba4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59b49428ee03-0002-0003",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "True, Hemphill cited one Sixth Amendment precedent, Crawford v. Washington, 541 U. S. 36 (2004), and stated that \u201cthe introduction of Morris's guilty plea minutes violated [his] Sixth Amendment right.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "59b49428ee030541a5a545308836d6a29999e9b1d0be7442b0acfea8b82e6ba4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59b49428ee03-0002-0004",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Reid represented \u201ca radical shift never adopted by\u201d the New York Court of Appeals in Reid or its progeny."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "59b49428ee030541a5a545308836d6a29999e9b1d0be7442b0acfea8b82e6ba4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59b49428ee03-0002-0005",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Rather, Hemphill lamented that, \u201c[a]s a practical matter,\u201d the Appellate Division's approach \u201ccreate[d] a minefeld for counsel in which the only way for the accused to rely on the rules of evidence or constitutional protections is to remain mute.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "59b49428ee030541a5a545308836d6a29999e9b1d0be7442b0acfea8b82e6ba4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59b49428ee03-0002-0006",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Court has excused the failure to present a federal claim in state court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "59b49428ee030541a5a545308836d6a29999e9b1d0be7442b0acfea8b82e6ba4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59b49428ee03-0002-0009",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Either way, the Court today purports to resolve what is effectively an intramural disagreement within the New York judiciary in order to reach a novel constitutional claim."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
